    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Lawrence Butler** (74.61) and **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (70.97) anchor the LawDog lineup as our premier plays. **Lawrence Butler** benefits immensely from a soft matchup against Randy Dobnak (xERA 4.70), where his dynamic platoon advantage (+13%) and placement in the cleanup spot project to maximize both R and RBI output. Similarly, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remains a plug-and-play elite option; despite a slight negative adjustment for facing a top-tier defensive catcher, his high floor and favorable order placement (#2) make him our most reliable engine for counting stats. **Daulton Varsho** (65.74) also earns a strong recommendation, leveraging a high-ceiling platoon advantage against Grayson Rodriguez to provide crucial versatility in our UTIL slot.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved balancing **Dylan Beavers** (55.70) against the high-leverage context of the remainder of the lineup. While **Dylan Beavers** carries significant risk facing an arm like Gerrit Cole, the extreme park factor (+16%) and his platoon edge keep him viable; he narrowly stayed in the starting nine over **Yainer Diaz** (54.87). **Yainer Diaz** was penalized heavily by his assumed #9 spot in the order, which mitigates the value of his matchup against Rodriguez. Elsewhere, we are proceeding with caution regarding **Jung Hoo Lee** (44.41); he is our weakest start today, as the matchup against a formidable Gavin Williams (xERA 2.99) significantly depresses his ceiling.\n\nRisk management remains critical as we navigate a slate where most lineups are still pending. We are closely monitoring the status of **Cal Raleigh**, whose score is highly sensitive to his position in the batting order; should he drop lower than the assumed #7 spot, his efficiency will dip further. Note that **Tyler Freeman** and **Will Smith** remain sidelined on the IL, while **Bryce Harper** and **Justin Crawford** are unavailable due to team off-days. We will be watching for late-breaking news regarding **Matt Chapman**, **Luis Arraez**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Gleyber Torres**, **Gavin Sheets**, **Alex Freeland**, and **Kyle Karros** to ensure we aren't leaving production on the table should any lineup shifts create an unexpected opening for our bench.",
